  "name": "Selkie Warden",
  "type": "subclass",
  "img": "modules/grimnir-lyonesse/assets/icons/lorc-wave-crest.svg",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Selkie Wardens are Rangers who have bound themselves to a selkie through possession of its seal skin. In claiming it, they do not merely command the selkie, but draw upon her nature, channeling the magic of the tides and the gift of transformation. This power is not freely given but shared through a bond neither of them can escape. Such a bond is never whole. The Selkie Warden feels the selkie’s longing as their own, while the selkie senses the Selkie Warden’s presence like a wound that will not close. Affection and resentment coil together, tightening with time. Most Selkie Wardens come to understand that closeness only deepens the torment, and so they keep their distance, refusing to indulge the bond. Selkie Wardens walk the line between love and control, between land and sea. The ocean remembers such bargains, and it always demands its due.</p>"
    },
    "source": {
      "custom": "Legends of the Round Table: Chivalric Handbook",
      "page": "56",
      "rules": "2024"
    },
